    "title": {
     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Ravi found that his answer to 2x + 3 = 11 gave x = 7 and the check failed.\n\"Mind the mistake, mend the mistake,\" said his teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "algebra",
     "Brahmagupta",
     "check"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Algebra grew from many places. Indian mathematicians like Brahmagupta and Aryabhata used symbols and rules for unknowns, and the word algebra comes from al-jabr, a term used by the Arab scholar al-Khwarizmi.\nCommon mistakes: forgetting to do the same on both sides, or mishandling signs. In 2x + 3 = 11 we subtract 3 to get 2x = 8, then divide by 2 to get x = 4.\nWe check by substituting back: 2 x 4 + 3 = 11, which is true."
    }
